### DKMS modules

Run `dkms status` and check each module's kernel pin (see references/hazard-checks.md). A
module whose pin excludes the target kernel will fail to build and can break boot (GPU /
network). Record at-risk modules here:

- [ ] `dkms status` reviewed; at-risk modules: _none found / list them_

### Autoremove candidates

Run `apt-get autoremove --purge -s` and classify per references/hazard-checks.md. Protect
third-party tools and binary-providers with `apt-mark manual` BEFORE any autoremove.
Record the protect list here:

- [ ] autoremove simulation reviewed; protect with `apt-mark manual`: _list packages_

### Foreign / local packages

Run `apt list --installed 2>/dev/null | grep -F '[installed,local]'` (see
references/hazard-checks.md). These are not updated by the upgrade; add a repo now or plan a
manual reinstall after.

- [ ] foreign packages reviewed; add repo before / reinstall after: _list packages_

## Phase 0 - Preconditions & backup

- [ ] Full, RESTORABLE backup confirmed (BorgMatic / image / snapshot)
- [ ] On AC power, stable wired network, enough time (1-2h)
- [ ] If over SSH: running inside screen/tmux (do-release-upgrade refuses a plain SSH
  session; it opens a backup sshd on port 1022)
- [ ] System readiness: free space (`df -h / /var /boot`, esp. /boot), no blocking
  held/pinned packages (`apt-mark showhold`), clean state (`sudo dpkg --audit`, `apt-get check`)
- [ ] Non-standard setup noted (encrypted/RAID disks, unusual mounts, services/DBs needing
  manual stop or backup): _none / list_
- [ ] Upgrade path open (see above)

## Phase 1 - Pre-flight inspection

- [ ] This runbook generated and reviewed with the user
